Let each half of the trip have distance \(d\). Total distance is \(2d\). Total time is \[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{d}{30}+\frac{d}{60}&=\frac{2d}{60}+\frac{d}{60} \\
&=\frac{3d}{60} \\
&=\frac{d}{20}
\end{aligned}
\]. Average speed is \(\frac{2d}{\frac{d}{20}}=40\text{ km}\text{/h}\).

For the cone, similar triangles give \(\frac{r}{h}=\frac{2}{4}=\frac{1}{2}\), so \(r=\frac{h}{2}\). Thus \[
\begin{aligned}
V&=\frac{1}{3}\pi r^2h \\
&=\frac{1}{3}\pi\left(\frac{h}{2}\right)^2h \\
&=\frac{\pi h^3}{12}
\end{aligned}
\]. Differentiating, \(\frac{dV}{dt}=\frac{\pi h^2}{4}\frac{dh}{dt}\). At \(h=4\) and \(\frac{dh}{dt}=-0.1\), \(\frac{dV}{dt}=\frac{\pi(16)}{4}(-0.1)=-0.4\pi\). The volume decreases at \(0.4\pi\text{ m}^3\text{/min}\).
